module std.compiler_entry

import std.measure {
  Nanosecond,
  nanosecond,
  nanosecond_count,
  millisecond,
  millisecond_to_nanosecond
}

// WHICH MODULE IS THE COMPILER PIPELINE ENTRY IS A FACT ABOUT THE MODULE, CARRIED BY IT.
//
// The emitter used to answer that question by comparing a module's authored name against the
// literal "v1.compiler.compile". That predicate does not name the property it is used for: v1's
// entry is v1.compiler.compile and v2's is v2.compiler.compile, so the literal distinguishes WHICH
// SEED GENERATION WROTE THE COMPILER, not whether a module is a compiler pipeline at all. It is a
// generation discriminator wearing a role predicate's name, and the repair that suggests itself --
// matching a second literal -- is the same defect twice: it breaks at the next generation and it
// hard-codes into the tool a fact about the corpus the tool reads.
//
// The question is DECIDABLE and FULLY MODELLED, so DESIGN section 5 puts it at wall-now:
// construction over validation, and the construction is that the entry module says so itself.
//
// THE DRIVER SHAPE IS A SECOND FACT AND IS NOT DERIVABLE FROM THE FIRST. DESIGN section 3 separates
// interface, realization and policy: "this module is the compiler pipeline entry" is the interface
// fact, and WHICH DRIVER REALIZES IT is realization. Three realizations exist in the tree today and
// all are load-bearing, so the sum below is closed at three rather than opened for futures nobody
// has. A fourth would have to be authored deliberately, which is the point of a closed vocabulary.
//
// RetainedHostCliKernel -- the seed's own entry: a clap CLI whose compile verb dispatches into
// hand-authored host Rust (v1_compiler.cli_run). Only a crate that CONTAINS that retained host
// source can select it, which is why the shape must be declared rather than assumed: a
// self-emitted compiler does not contain cli_run, so rendering this driver for it would emit a
// main naming a module that is not there -- trading a correct refusal for a call that does not
// link.
//
// DirectIngestDriver -- a driver that reaches the emitted compiler's own ingest entry, taking
// source text and a target and returning emitted text, with no retained host kernel between them.
// ONE SOURCE, NO PEERS, SYNTHETIC SUBJECT: it is a census instrument for the standalone native
// front door, not a repository execution route -- a module whose imports resolve only against
// sibling roots cannot pass through it.
//
// SourceRootEvalDriver -- the repository test-execution route. The rendered main reads a universe
// of qualified test identities (module path + declaration name, one per line) and the declared
// source roots, builds the SourceRootIngest itself (the filesystem read is the host boundary the
// driver owns), then hands the whole ingest to the pipeline: assemble the context ONCE, prepare
// (resolve + infer) once per unique module, and per universe member Eval the named declaration,
// reporting one typed verdict row per member. This is the driver the required-v2-native CI lane
// executes; its contract is that every universe member reaches exactly one terminal observation,
// never a silent remainder. The process re-derives its own exclusive wall partition on stderr
// as `[native-cost-partition]` (same receipt shape as claim_batch `[cost-partition]`: the rows
// NativeDriverExclusiveRows carries, over parent_span_nanos) plus one `[native-prepare-split]`
// line per unique module that partitions prepare into resolve vs infer (the two halves
// native_test_resolve_module / native_test_infer_resolved) and carries decls=. Its outcome names
// which arm decided the module: accepted, infer_refused, resolve_refused, or context_refused --
// the last for a module whose FILE this context already refused, which never enters the resolver,
// so its resolve span is the refusal lookup and not a resolution it did not perform. The
// `[native-cost-partition]` verdict is native_driver_cost_account over NativeDriverExclusiveRows,
// not a second copy of the reconcile law: remainder_nanos is that fold's residual, and
// OverAttributed carries no remainder field (underflow is not a number). A non-Reconciled
// arm is a process refusal, not a printed string with exit 0. Re-run the emitted binary over
// a universe file to re-derive the numbers.

type CompilerEntryDriver
  = RetainedHostCliKernel
  | DirectIngestDriver
  | SourceRootEvalDriver

// MODULE RELEASE IS ITS OWN ROW BECAUSE RELEASE IS NOT FREE AND WAS NOT ATTRIBUTED. The per-module
// loop closed its prepare span and then let the module's resolved tree fall out of scope at the end
// of the iteration, so freeing it was paid inside parent_span and covered by no row.
//
// WHAT THIS ROW DOES NOT EXPLAIN, CORRECTED BY MEASUREMENT. An earlier version of this paragraph
// said the full corpus's residual WAS this release cost. That was a hypothesis written as history
// and it is false: measured on the full corpus, module_release is 1.9 ms while the residual stood
// at 244.8 ms, and a third fold measured 1.86 ms against 238.8 ms. The row is real, measured and
// non-overlapping, and it accounts for roughly one part in a hundred of what was unattributed. The
// span that does account for it is relay_emit below. A row placed around the wrong span leaves the
// residual intact while the class reads as repaired, which is why the correction is recorded here
// rather than quietly replaced.
//
// RELAY EMIT IS THE PER-MODULE RECEIPT LINE, and it was outside every span. The loop prints one
// [native-prepare-split] line per unique module to stderr, which the host runner drains through a
// pipe, and that write was paid inside parent_span with no row over it.
//
// WHAT THE FOLDS MEASURED, BY FOLD, FROM THE [native-cost-partition] LINE OF EACH RUN. The figure
// is remainder_nanos divided by unique_modules on that same line; re-derive it by reading the line
// rather than trusting this list:
//   SUCC3  45a9105101   238,500,502 ns / 714 = 334.0 us per unique module
//   SUCC6  4011bf9d     244,833,742 ns / 714 = 342.9 us
//   #11256 f5e8a568     238,817,913 ns / 714 = 334.5 us
//   #11202 a3157d6a     276,596,559 ns / 717 = 385.8 us
// THAT IS A 15.5% SPREAD AND NOT A CONSTANT. An earlier version of this paragraph called it a
// per-module constant on the first three folds; the fourth refutes that, and calling it constant
// would repeat in this very annotation the defect the paragraph above it records. The spread is
// consistent with a pipe write whose cost tracks line length and the reader's drain rate, and
// consistent-with is not established-by: relay_emit exists to settle it by measurement.
//
// BOTH ROWS ARE MEASURED AROUND THE WORK, never derived as parent minus the others -- a row defined
// as the remainder forces the residual to zero and makes the tolerance arm unfireable, which is the
// defect this partition exists to catch.
// THE NATIVE DRIVER'S EXCLUSIVE WALL PARTITION. claim_batch prints `[cost-partition]` over
// resolve-span work; SourceRootEvalDriver prints `[native-cost-partition]` over its own
// single-threaded wall. The grains are the driver's own, not a restatement of the resolve-split
// rows, and THIS TYPE IS WHERE THEY ARE NAMED: the row set below is the grain, so prose that
// re-lists the field names would be a second spelling of it that rots the moment a driver gains
// a phase. The law is the same exclusive-sum law: exclusive rows must not exceed parent_span,
// and the remainder (parent minus exclusive) must sit inside the declared tolerance or the
// receipt is not a partition. Durations are std.measure Nanosecond (Time/Nano), not a bare Int
// whose unit lives only in the field name. Re-derive by running the emitted binary; these rows
// are the type of that stderr JSON, not a second ledger.
//
// WHY THE ROW SET IS A SUPERSET OF ANY ONE DRIVER'S PHASES. A driver reports zero for a phase it
// does not have, and that zero is a fact about the driver rather than a gap in the law: the sum
// and the tolerance check are unchanged by a zero row, so one law folds every driver. The route
// that DERIVES its universe from source roots pays two phases a driver handed a universe file
// cannot have -- universe_derivation (discovery, the import-closure walk, and the ingest
// identity join, whose scanned-versus-ingested populations are what closure-scoped ingest is
// judged by) and receipt_admission (minting the receipt and adjudicating it). They are members
// of the exclusive sum like any other row, so an over-attribution routed through either is
// caught by native_driver_cost_account and not by a second check.
//
// row_serialization IS A MEASURED SPAN AND NOT THE RESIDUAL, and the distinction is the whole
// reason it exists rather than a widened tolerance. Serializing each observation to JSON and
// writing it to stdout is real work the driver performs and no other row covers: it sits outside
// eval, which is the sum of the identity fold and nothing else. It went unattributed until the
// tolerance arm became a refusal and the route's own full-N run refused on it -- residual
// 158600186 ns against a 50000000 ns tolerance, about 45 us per identity across 3544 identities.
//
// DEFINING IT AS "whatever is left" WOULD HAVE BEEN THE FABRICATION, not the fix: a row equal to
// parent minus the others makes the sum identically equal to the parent, the residual identically
// zero, and NativeDriverCostRemainderExceedsTolerance unfireable by construction -- a check that
// cannot fail, which DESIGN section 5 calls worse than absent because it will be cited as
// coverage. So the driver times the serialize-and-write span with its own clock reads, the
// residual is measured again afterwards, and if a residual still exceeds the tolerance the answer
// is to NAME THE NEXT UNATTRIBUTED SPAN, never to widen the tolerance to fit.

// SCRATCH BISECT ROWS (not for landing): bisect_row_accumulation, bisect_loop_setup, and the
// partitioning pair bisect_arm_exit and bisect_driver_tail. THE SECOND PAIR IS NOT A GUESS AT A
// CULPRIT -- it is a partition. Three hypotheses for the remainder have now been measured and
// refuted (module_release, relay_emit, and the clock apparatus, the last falsified by a direct
// 35 ns/call measurement on the fold host), so these two spans cover the ONLY regions left
// uncovered by construction rather than naming a fourth suspect: bisect_arm_exit is the
// iteration body from the match's close to the release span, which is where the match arm's
// bindings drop; bisect_driver_tail is from the row-serialization close to the parent close.
// Between them they answer WHICH HALF the remainder lives in -- inside the per-module loop or
// outside it -- whichever way they land, in one fold instead of two.
//
// THE FIRST PAIR, and what it established. TWO
// non-overlapping spans around the only work in the per-module iteration that no exclusive row
// covers, added to read ONE full fold and find which carries the ~240 ms remainder. A third span
// around the "iteration tail" was written and then deleted: as written it opened and closed with
// nothing between it, so it could only ever read zero -- a decoration, and the interval it meant
// to cover is already the tail half of bisect_loop_setup, which spans one iteration's end to the
// next prepare open.
type NativeDriverExclusiveRows {
  load: Nanosecond
  universe_derivation: Nanosecond
  context: Nanosecond
  prepare: Nanosecond
  eval: Nanosecond
  receipt_admission: Nanosecond
  row_serialization: Nanosecond
  module_release: Nanosecond
  relay_emit: Nanosecond
  bisect_row_accumulation: Nanosecond
  bisect_loop_setup: Nanosecond
  bisect_arm_exit: Nanosecond
  bisect_driver_tail: Nanosecond
}

type NativeDriverCostAccounting
  = NativeDriverCostReconciled { residual: Nanosecond, tolerance: Nanosecond }
  | NativeDriverCostOverAttributed { sum_exclusive: Nanosecond, parent_span: Nanosecond }
  | NativeDriverCostRemainderExceedsTolerance { residual: Nanosecond, tolerance: Nanosecond }

// Fifty milliseconds on the host monotonic wall Instant the driver uses. A remainder larger
// than this is unattributed driver work, not a rounding crumb.
data native_driver_cost_remainder_tolerance_nanos: Nanosecond = millisecond_to_nanosecond(m: millisecond(count: 50))

fn native_driver_exclusive_sum(rows: NativeDriverExclusiveRows) -> Nanosecond {
  nanosecond(count: nanosecond_count(n: rows.load) + nanosecond_count(n: rows.universe_derivation) + nanosecond_count(n: rows.context) + nanosecond_count(n: rows.prepare) + nanosecond_count(n: rows.eval) + nanosecond_count(n: rows.receipt_admission) + nanosecond_count(n: rows.row_serialization) + nanosecond_count(n: rows.module_release) + nanosecond_count(n: rows.relay_emit) + nanosecond_count(n: rows.bisect_row_accumulation) + nanosecond_count(n: rows.bisect_loop_setup) + nanosecond_count(n: rows.bisect_arm_exit) + nanosecond_count(n: rows.bisect_driver_tail))
}

fn native_driver_cost_account(
  parent_span: Nanosecond,
  exclusive: NativeDriverExclusiveRows,
  tolerance: Nanosecond
) -> NativeDriverCostAccounting {
  let sum = native_driver_exclusive_sum(rows: exclusive)
  if nanosecond_count(n: sum) > nanosecond_count(n: parent_span) {
    NativeDriverCostOverAttributed {
      sum_exclusive: sum,
      parent_span: parent_span
    }
  } else {
    let residual = nanosecond(count: nanosecond_count(n: parent_span) - nanosecond_count(n: sum))
    if nanosecond_count(n: residual) > nanosecond_count(n: tolerance) {
      NativeDriverCostRemainderExceedsTolerance {
        residual: residual,
        tolerance: tolerance
      }
    } else {
      NativeDriverCostReconciled {
        residual: residual,
        tolerance: tolerance
      }
    }
  }
}

// DECLARED FRONTIER (DESIGN §3c) — not a live bind on this head.
// native_driver_cost_row_standing has no executing consumer here: planted witnesses
// prove the fold; they do not exercise the spawn. Consumer: native_lane_runner
// run_native_binary. Route: after the child exits, that spawn reads the relayed
// stderr into NativeDriverChildExited and folds native_driver_cost_row_standing,
// refusing NativeDriverCostRowsUnobserved. Trigger (DESIGN §4b(3) capability, not
// an artifact): the host relays the child's stderr on successful exit
// (native_lane_runner run_native_binary as changed by #10940). Kill condition: if
// that relay lands and this standing is still unread, the row is dangling. Until
// the capability holds, this PR stays off native_lane_runner (deep-cat-655 owns
// it). Observed is [native-cost-partition] after exit; Unobserved is exited
// without that tag; Pending is the child still running. On main, Command::output
// drops the pipe on success (eager-raven-113 #11060 universe receipt: 15508s
// admitted, 3536 verdict rows, zero partition tags in host-captured stderr). The
// relay is exit-gated, not streamed.

type NativeDriverChildStanding
  = NativeDriverChildExited { stderr: String }
  | NativeDriverChildStillRunning

type NativeDriverCostRowStanding
  = NativeDriverCostRowsObserved
  | NativeDriverCostRowsUnobserved
  | NativeDriverCostRowsPending

fn native_driver_cost_row_standing(child: NativeDriverChildStanding) -> NativeDriverCostRowStanding {
  match child {
    NativeDriverChildStillRunning => NativeDriverCostRowsPending
    NativeDriverChildExited { stderr } =>
      if string_contains(s: stderr, pattern: "[native-cost-partition] ") {
        NativeDriverCostRowsObserved
      } else {
        NativeDriverCostRowsUnobserved
      }
  }
}
